# Byte-stable text assets across platforms (2026-11-21 audit).
#
# The Windows CI runners check out with git's `core.autocrlf=true`
# default, which rewrites every text file to CRLF in the working tree.
# That must not reach bytes that are semantically load-bearing:
#
# - `mochy-innertube/assets/solver/*.js` are vendored upstream artifacts
#   whose integrity is asserted by checksum (byte-identity with the
#   pinned Android baseline and the official npm builds) and are
#   compiled into the binary via include_str!;
# - `tests/fixtures/` is replayed byte-for-byte by the offline suites.
#
# This was investigated as a candidate root cause of the Windows EJS
# test failure and ruled out (CRLF fixtures still pass), but the
# normalization removes the whole class of working-tree divergence
# between platforms. Rust source, manifests and CI config are pinned to
# LF as well — rustfmt's output — so a Windows checkout builds and
# formats identically to Linux/macOS.
*.js  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.rs  text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.lock text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
